  "reason": "Only one experiment (config_001: RNA-only, singleprofile, pca_n2000, acc=0.485) is completed, so evidence is extremely sparse. The most critical unresolved question for a multimodal cellular profiling study is whether adding the image modality to the RNA baseline provides any benefit. config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the minimal extension of config_001: it keeps the same RNA encoder and profile setting, and only adds the image branch with the simplest fusion (concat). This directly isolates the effect of the image modality against the existing baseline. If it outperforms 0.485, it validates the multimodal direction and justifies further exploration of fusion/aggregation/encoder choices; if it does not, it saves budget from pursuing the 36 multimodal configs. Testing image_only (config_010) would be less efficient because it would still require a subsequent multimodal experiment to answer the same core question, consuming an extra budget slot."
}

